  'Displaced tracks (charged tracks that do not point back to the collision, as produced by b-hadron decays): making all tracks prompt (displacement set to zero) lowers the share of H→bb̄ jets called H→bb̄ from 92 % to 10 %. Shrinking every displacement by a factor 0.35 keeps 86 % of these calls, but keeping only two displaced tracks lowers it to 32 %. So ParT responds to how many displaced tracks there are rather than to how far they travel. '
