H56_EXPLAINER = [
 ('Question', "Are three earlier results properties of training on top or quark/gluon labels, and how much do they move between two trainings that differ only in the random seed? (i) the direction part of the axis-convention response (H36/H39, claim D4m), (ii) the jet-charge response (H40/H42, claim D16), (iii) the small response to particle count at fixed IRC-safe energy flow (H24v, claim D7).", None),
 ('Physics background', "Recomputing particle coordinates about the winner-take-all (WTA) or hardest-particle (HP) axis is a rigid translation by the axis offset $\\delta_j$. The direction part is $D=\\langle \\mathbf 1[\\text{call changes about the axis}]-\\tfrac1{20}\\sum_k \\mathbf 1[\\text{call changes under a shift of length }|\\delta_j|\\text{ in direction }k]\\rangle$ in percentage points. An exact collinear split replaces one soft particle by two with half its $p_T$ each at the same $(y,\\phi)$: $N\\to N+1$ while every IRC-safe observable is unchanged, so a response to it is a response to $N$ beyond IRC-safe energy flow. A likelihood ratio in $N$ alone, LR($N$), gives $+0.10$ log-odds per particle.", None),
 ('Method', "Per architecture (ParT, ParticleNet, PFN, EFN): seed 0, a second seed (same data and settings), a shuffled-label training (label = hash of jet $(p_T,\\eta,\\phi)$ mod 2) and 6 untrained (epoch-0) networks. Axis: Top Landscape (seed 3901) and QG Pythia (seed 3911) test jets, 10,000 each; calls at the sign of the log-odds and at signal efficiency 0.3 and 0.5. Count: 3,998 Pythia jets (seed 7243), slope over $k=1..5$ of the logit change under $k$ exact splits minus that under a $\\Delta N=0$ control. 95 % jet bootstrap; paired sign-flip and McNemar tests for seed 1 vs seed 0; Holm over 283 tests. The charge step was not run: the four particle-ID trainings were killed for memory at 40 GiB and are rerunning at 48 GiB.", None),
 ('Result', "Accuracies seed 0 / 1: Top ParticleNet 94.05 / 94.05 %, QG ParT 82.45 / 82.53 % (epoch 16), QG PFN 81.70 / 81.15 %; every shuffled-label network ended at a constant output (50 %). Axis: no seed-0 or seed-1 cell lies outside the untrained band after Holm; the sign agrees in 38 of 42 cells; $D$ moves by up to 1–2 pp between seeds (QG PFN, $\\varepsilon_S=0.5$, HP: $+1.16\\to+0.08$). Count: ParT_kin $+0.0079$ / $+0.0063$, ParticleNet_kin $+0.0042$ / $+0.0042$ log-odds per particle (seed 0 / 1), against LR($N$) $+0.10$; EFN split response 0.", 'results/physics/h56_seed_nulls.png'),
 ('Checks', "Seed-0 rows reproduce H39 and H24v on the same samples; the axis edit equals a shift of the stored arrays; seed-1 accuracies within 0.6 pp of seed 0. The verifier's rerun on new jets with 12–20 untrained networks per architecture is in the next entry.", None),
 ('Physical significance', "The extra response of trained taggers to shifting the jet toward its WTA or hardest-particle axis is no larger than the difference between two trainings or the spread of untrained networks. The small residual response to particle number at fixed energy flow (4–8 % of a pure counter) repeats across seeds. Networks trained on unrelated labels learn a constant and cannot serve as a null with spread.", None),
]

