H65_EXPLAINER = [
 ('Question', "If a jet is covered by a uniform haze of soft particles, like pileup or underlying event, do neural taggers degrade like a plain-mass cut, like a groomed-mass cut, like an area-subtracted mass, or like a particle counter?", None),
 ('Physics background', "Diffuse contamination of density $\\rho$ adds $p_T\\approx\\rho A$ to a jet of area $A$ and raises its mass roughly as $\\delta m^2\\approx\\rho A\\,p_{T,J}\\langle\\Delta R^2\\rangle$. Soft drop declusters the jet until $\\min(p_{T1},p_{T2})/(p_{T1}+p_{T2})>z_{\\rm cut}$ and so drops soft wide-angle particles. Area subtraction removes the expected contribution, $p^\\mu_{\\rm sub}=p^\\mu_J-\\rho A^\\mu$. A count-based tagger responds to $\\Delta N\\approx\\rho A/\\langle p_T\\rangle$ wherever the particles land.", None),
 ('Method', "Massless ghosts with $p_T\\in[0.5,1]$ GeV, uniform over the jet disc, $\\rho\\in\\{2,5,10,20\\}$ GeV per unit area, the same positions for every model; input axis fixed. Controls with the same ghosts: c1 (one particle with the summed $p_T$ at the axis), c2 (all ghosts stacked at the axis: count up, mass almost unchanged), in / out (only where soft drop keeps or removes them). Samples: hls4ml, JetClass W/Z/top/QCD, Top Landscape, QG, 2,000 per class. References at 50 % signal efficiency: plain-$m$, $m_{SD}$ and $m_{\\rm sub}$ windows, LR($N$), EFN. Metrics: $\\varepsilon_S(\\rho)$, $\\Delta s$, stacked share $\\Delta s(c2)/\\Delta s(pu)$, $r_{\\Delta s}=\\Delta s(out)/\\Delta s(in)$.", None),
 ('Result', "W efficiency at $\\rho$ = 10: JEDI-linear 0.00, JetClass ParT_full 0.10, against 0.47 for the hls4ml $m_{SD}$ window (its $m_{\\rm sub}$ window 0.12–0.20 over $\\rho$) and 0.43–0.46 for the JetClass $m_{SD}$ and $m_{\\rm sub}$ windows; Top ParT 0.24 (m_SD 0.40). Stacked share: JEDI-linear 0.01 (mass reader), JetClass ParT_full W 1.17, Top ParT 1.22, QG ParT 0.16. Out/in: JEDI-linear 3.22 (as the plain-mass window), ParT_full W 0.53, Top ParT 0.39, QG ParT 4.6. Left panel: a JetClass W jet with 27 ghosts, $m$ 80 → 101 GeV, $m_{SD}$ 79 → 79 GeV.", 'results/physics/h65_pileup.png'),
 ('Checks', "Unedited accuracies reproduce (JEDI-linear 0.815, Top ParT AUC 0.987, QG ParT 0.901). The IRC-safe EFN gives c2 = c1. Permuted and untrained nulls $\\Delta s\\approx0$, except the permuted PFN (sum pooling counts by construction). The on-axis stack gives out-of-range outputs (3–74 log-odds) for ParticleNet_kin and LorentzNet and is not read for them. The hls4ml 64-slot input keeps only 40–81 % of the ghosts.", None),
 ('Physical significance', "No network behaves like a groomed or area-corrected mass under diffuse soft contamination. The hls4ml tagger's sensitivity is the plain-mass shift; the larger JetClass and Top taggers respond to soft particles added without mass (for JetClass ParT_full mostly through their particle-ID label, H65v); quark–gluon taggers respond mostly to wide-angle particles.", None),
]

