 ('Method', "JetClass test file _100, 1,000 random rows per class (rng 6801). Each particle keeps $(p_x,p_y,p_z,E)$; only its type flags change, and neutral particles get charge 0 and zero impact parameters as Delphes stores them. fr05/10/20: random charged hadrons carrying 5/10/20 % of the jet energy → neutral hadrons; frg10 → photons; ph2nh, nh2ph: all photons ↔ neutral hadrons. Score $\\Delta s=\\langle(\\ell_c-\\ell_{\\rm QCD})_{\\rm edit}-(\\ell_c-\\ell_{\\rm QCD})_{\\rm orig}\\rangle_{\\text{class }c}$. Controls: charge-sign swap (c_same), ParT_kin / PN_kin (no type inputs), 6 permuted ParT_full. References: LR($f_{ch}$), GBDT on $(m,\\tau_{21},\\tau_{32},N,f_{ch},f_{nh},f_\\gamma)$. Ghost arm: added soft particles with the measured soft composition (74 % photons), single labels, stacked and clustered.", None),
 ('Result', "ParT_full fr10: $-0.16$ to $-1.00$ log-odds over the nine signal classes (Hbb $-0.46\\,[-0.52,-0.40]$), linear in the moved fraction; ph2nh $-0.85$ to $-2.55$; kinematics-only models exactly 0. The fraction-aware GBDT agrees in sign for 5/9 classes. Ghosts at $\\rho=10$: ParT_full W $-2.78$ with the measured composition vs ParT_kin $-2.85$; stacked share 0.39. Left: the fr10 set on a real H→bb jet.", 'results/physics/h68_particle_type.png'),
 ('Checks', "Unedited 10-class accuracy ParT_full 0.861, PN_full 0.842 (known 0.859 / 0.846). The jitter control c_kin gives 0 for every model, but as a zero-mean jitter it cannot bound a kinematic response (H68v). The charge-sign swap moves the scores by up to $-0.61$, so it is not a null.", None),
